melonDS: hotkeys for save state, load state, next/previous state slot and quit

The Qt frontend saves and loads states only through its menu, whose fixed shortcuts are
Shift+F1..F8 / F1..F8, F9 and F12. Five new hotkeys (Keyboard/Joystick HK_SaveState,
HK_LoadState, HK_NextStateSlot, HK_PrevStateSlot, HK_Quit, unbound by default) act on a
current slot (1-8, shown in the OSD), so the same keys as every other Kettle emulator work.
Once either state hotkey is bound to a key, the menu items lose their F-key shortcuts, which
would otherwise clash (F2 loading slot 2).

